    qForQ: [
      { starter: 'I feel like I\'m wasting my potential.', reply: 'What would it look like to live up to it — not the version someone else imagined, but yours?', tip: 'Separate their potential from the expectations projected onto them!' },
      { starter: 'I don\'t know if the choices I\'m making are right.', reply: 'What values would make the decision feel right — regardless of the outcome?', tip: 'Shift from outcome-based to values-based thinking through a question!' },
      { starter: 'Nobody talks about what really matters.', reply: 'What do you wish someone would ask you that nobody ever does?', tip: 'Use a meta-question to invite the real conversation!' },
      { starter: 'I\'m terrified of getting it wrong.', reply: 'If you were guaranteed you\'d learn something valuable from getting it wrong — what would you try first?', tip: 'Reframe the cost of failure with a single question!' },
      { starter: 'Everything feels performative.', reply: 'When was the last time something felt completely real and unperformed — what was happening?', tip: 'Ground the abstract in a specific memory through a question!' },
      { starter: 'I don\'t know who I am without external validation.', reply: 'If every opinion of you vanished tonight — what would remain?', tip: 'Strip away the scaffolding with a question that asks what\'s underneath!' },
      { starter: 'I\'m afraid I\'ll look back and regret this time.', reply: 'What would the version of you who doesn\'t regret it have done differently — starting this week?', tip: 'Make the desired future concrete and actionable through a question!' },
      { starter: 'I\'m not sure if I believe in anything anymore.', reply: 'What is one thing — even small — that you find yourself defending when someone attacks it?', tip: 'Find the value through the thing they are willing to protect!' },
      { starter: 'I feel like the world is going in the wrong direction.', reply: 'If you could move one dial — anywhere — what would you adjust first, and who would it affect?', tip: 'A specific action question cuts through paralysis better than a general worry question!' },
      { starter: 'I\'m overwhelmed by how much there is to learn.', reply: 'If you could only know one thing really deeply — more than most people on Earth — what would you choose?', tip: 'Narrowing the frame can make the infinite feel manageable!' },
      { starter: 'I want to make a difference but don\'t know how.', reply: 'What is the smallest meaningful action you could take this week that is completely within your control?', tip: 'The distance between intention and action often closes with one specific question!' },
      { starter: 'I feel disconnected from most people I know.', reply: 'Who in your life — even just one person — actually makes you feel more yourself, not less? What do they do differently?', tip: 'Anchor the abstract to a specific relationship to make it real!' },
    ],
